0..77 Comment "// The circle and the integers without a higher inductive type. The circle is"
78..153 Comment "// presented by a point, a loop and its inverse, with the two cancellations"
154..228 Comment "// as rules; its shape is a signature. The integers are presented the same"
229..303 Comment "// way, so they model the shape with laws that are conversion: the winding"
304..379 Comment "// number folds the circle into them, and spinning folds them back. A model"
380..452 Comment "// over the native integers stands beside it with its laws owed, and the"
453..514 Comment "// winding number into it is a fold that rests on those laws."
516..593 Comment "/// The circle as a presented type: its rules rewrite constructor terms, so a"
594..636 Comment "/// word normalizes to the loops it winds."
637..639 Other "@["
640..650 Other "normalizes"
